<subpara id="RM0000026XZ01AX_06" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I2C00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<topic>
<title>Confirmation Driving</title>
<ptxt>By performing confirmation driving, it is possible to check whether the DTC is reproduced.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A179391J02" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</topic>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) display screen, clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000CCX015X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Start the engine, turn all accessory switches OFF, and warm up the engine until the engine coolant temperature stabilizes. (Engine coolant temperature 75°C or higher) (A)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Idle the engine for 15 minutes or more. (B)</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Check [ECU Data Monitor] - [Purge Rate] on SST (TaSCAN). DTC judgment is performed when this value is in the range of 5 to 95%.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, check the DTC judgment result. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000CCX015X"/>)</ptxt>
<atten2>
<ptxt>When performing this driving test, be sure to obey speed limits and other traffic laws.</ptxt>
</atten2>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the DTC judgment result is "judging" or "cannot judge", drive the vehicle at 40 to 60 km/h for 10 minutes or more (C), then check the DTC judgment result.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</item>
</list1>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000026XZ01AX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I2400000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>Inspect the fuses for circuits related to this system before performing the following troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), read the Freeze Frame Data. The Freeze Frame Data records part of the engine operating condition when the malfunction occurred, and this information is useful when troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000026XZ01AX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000026XZ01AX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I2500000">
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (Purge VSV)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [Active Test] - [Purge VSV].</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>[System Selection Screen: Powertrain → TCCS → Active Test]</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Restrictions</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Purge VSV</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Energize/de-energize purge VSV (vacuum switching valve assembly No.1)</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Duty ratio when energized 30%)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the 2 vacuum hoses of vacuum switching valve assembly No.1.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Operate vacuum switching valve assembly No.1.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A159587J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Apply positive pressure to port E and check whether air passes through.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.10in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Active Test</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Purge VSV)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Specified Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Air passes from port E to port F</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Air does not pass from port E to port F</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>NG</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>OK</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000026XZ01AX_04_0002" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM0000026XZ01AX_04_0005" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000026XZ01AX_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I2600000">
<testtitle>Inspect Vacuum Switching Valve Assembly NO.1</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the vacuum switching valve assembly No.1 inspection procedure, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000020W4008X"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000026XZ01AX_04_0003" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000026XZ01AX_04_0006" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000026XZ01AX_04_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I2700000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Vacuum Switching Valve Assembly NO.1 Power Source Voltage)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D705AX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the vacuum switching valve assembly No.1 connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A194112J16" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the terminals.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.48in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.82in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
<ptxt>Vacuum switching valve assembly No.1 vehicle side connector - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<table>
<title>Text in Illustrations</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.41in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.72in"/>
